title: 'statement-store: disconnect a peer that stops reading statements'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    A peer whose last two statement sends failed has stopped reading and is now disconnected.
    There is no reputation change, because such a peer is broken or overloaded, not malicious.
    A send left over from a previous connection does not count. When the peer reconnects it gets
    a fresh initial sync, and in the meantime routing sends new statements to other peers.
    Before, such a peer kept its connection and lost every chunk sent to it.

    A full propagation outbox now refuses new hashes instead of dropping its oldest. A full
    outbox alone disconnects nobody: a peer that is still reading keeps its connection and loses
    only the refused hashes, counted in
    `substrate_sync_statement_undelivered_total{reason="outbox_full"}`.

    Each disconnect is logged with the peer id and counted in
    `substrate_sync_statement_stalled_peers_disconnected`.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
